Chapter: LirCallCross

 The shapes, and what each is here to move:

  - callplain:  a call with its arguments already in place
  - callswap:   the arguments crossed, so the two moves form a CYCLE and the
                planner has to stage one through the scratch register
  - callimm-l / callimm-r: an immediate argument on each side
  - callres:    the result feeds arithmetic, so it is read out of x0
  - callchain:  a value live ACROSS a call, which the crossing analysis must
                place in the callee-saved pool or lose
  - callcond:   a call in each arm of a returning `if`
  - callthree / callthree2: three arguments, rotated two different ways

Section: Helpers

  hdiff : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  hdiff (a) (b) = if a >= b then a - b else 0 - (b - a)

  htri : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  htri (a) (b) (c) = if a > 0 then a * 100 + b * 10 + c else b * 10 + c

Section: Callers

  callplain : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  callplain (x) (y) = hdiff x y

  callswap : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  callswap (x) (y) = hdiff y x

  callimm-l : Integer -> Integer
  callimm-l (x) = hdiff 7 x

  callimm-r : Integer -> Integer
  callimm-r (x) = hdiff x 7

  callres : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  callres (x) (y) = hdiff x y + 1

  callchain : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  callchain (x) (y) = hdiff (hdiff x y) (hdiff y x)

  callcond : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  callcond (x) (y) = if x > 0 then hdiff x y else hdiff y x

  callthree : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  callthree (a) (b) (c) = htri c a b

  callthree2 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  callthree2 (a) (b) (c) = htri b c a

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (show (callplain 9 4))
   print-line-uni (show (callswap 9 4))
   print-line-uni (show (callimm-l 10))
   print-line-uni (show (callimm-r 10))
   print-line-uni (show (callres 9 4))
   print-line-uni (show (callchain 9 4))
   print-line-uni (show (callcond 9 4))
   print-line-uni (show (callcond (-9) 4))
   print-line-uni (show (callthree 1 2 3))
   print-line-uni (show (callthree2 1 2 3))
  end
